            (See Remark 12.2 of
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a{:href => "#AveryLeinster"} Avery and Leinster
          %h2#examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                The envelope of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Isbell+duality"} Isbell duality
                adjunction associated to a category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Isbell+envelope"} Isbell envelope
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                (called the
                %em category of gaps
                in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                by
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a{:href => "#PavlovicHughes"} Pavlovic and Hughes
            %li
              %p
                The envelope of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nuclear+adjunction"} nuclear adjunction
                associated to the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Isbell+duality"} Isbell duality
                adjunction for a small category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                is what
                %a{:href => "#PavlovicHughes"} Pavlovic and Hughes
                call the
                %em category of intervals
                in
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
